          "concept": "A Vue component is a reusable piece of UI with its own template, data, and logic, and a parent passes data down to it through props. Props are declared by the child with defineProps and are read-only: the child must never mutate a prop directly, because the parent owns that data. This one-way flow keeps data changes predictable in large apps. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Vue components and props — study it before you start the exercise.",
