          "concept": "A child talks back to its parent by emitting a custom event with a name and an optional payload, and the parent listens with v-on. The child never changes parent data directly; it announces that something happened and lets the parent decide what to do. This keeps the same one-way data flow as props, just in the opposite direction. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Vue custom events — study it before you start the exercise.",
