          "concept": "Template-driven forms build the form model from the template itself: ngModel binds an input to a property, and Angular tracks validity from the HTML attributes. Adding required to an input makes the control invalid until it is filled, and the form's valid flag drives the submit button. This style is quick for simple forms, but the model lives in the template, so complex validation gets awkward. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Angular template-driven forms — study it before you start the exercise.",
