          "concept": "A Svelte child talks to its parent with createEventDispatcher, which returns a dispatch function for custom events. The child calls dispatch('select', item) and the parent listens with on:select, receiving the payload in event.detail. DOM events such as on:click work directly on elements, and Svelte's event modifiers — once, preventDefault, stopPropagation — replace the boilerplate other frameworks need. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Svelte event dispatcher — study it before you start the exercise.",
