          "concept": "Svelte's bind: directive creates two-way binding between a form input and a variable: typing updates the variable, and changing the variable updates the input. The same syntax binds component props, so a parent can share a value with a child that edits it. Because Svelte compiles the binding, there is no runtime two-way-binding system to learn — it is just an assignment in both directions. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Svelte two-way binding — study it before you start the exercise.",
