          "introduction": "Transitions and Animations is a core skill in Svelte. Svelte's transitions animate elements as they enter and leave the DOM, and the syntax is a directive: transition:fade or in:fly and out:slide. In this lesson you will practise Svelte transitions and animations with small, runnable examples.",
          "concept": "Svelte's transitions animate elements as they enter and leave the DOM, and the syntax is a directive: transition:fade or in:fly and out:slide. Because the compiler knows when an element is added or removed, transitions need no extra state or CSS classes. The animate: directive handles list reordering, smoothly moving items to their new positions when the list changes. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Svelte transitions and animations — study it before you start the exercise.",
