          "concept": "Node's http module creates a server with a request handler that receives every request and a response object to answer it. The handler reads req.method and req.url, sets a status code and headers on res, and ends the response with res.end. This is the foundation Express is built on, and writing one by hand makes Express's conveniences obvious instead of magical. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Node.js HTTP servers — study it before you start the exercise.",
