          "concept": "npm is Node's package manager, and package.json is the manifest that lists a project's dependencies, scripts, and metadata. npm install reads the manifest and fills node_modules, while npm run executes the scripts — start, test, build — that the project defines. The lock file pins exact versions so every install reproduces the same tree, which is what keeps 'works on my machine' away. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with npm and package.json — study it before you start the exercise.",
