          "introduction": "Environment Variables and Configuration is a core skill in Node.js. Environment variables configure an app without changing its code, and Node reads them from process.env. In this lesson you will practise Node.js environment variables with small, runnable examples.",
          "concept": "Environment variables configure an app without changing its code, and Node reads them from process.env. A .env file holds local values during development and is loaded by a library such as dotenv, but it must never be committed, because secrets in version control are secrets shared with the world. Production sets real variables in the deployment environment instead. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Node.js environment variables — study it before you start the exercise.",
