          "concept": "Error-handling middleware has four arguments — err, req, res, next — and Express calls it whenever a handler passes an error to next(err) or throws in an async handler. It belongs at the end of the middleware chain so it catches everything above it, and it turns errors into a consistent JSON response with the right status code. Without one, Express sends a bare HTML error page and may leak a stack trace. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Express error-handling middleware — study it before you start the exercise.",
