          "concept": "Query strings carry optional filters in the URL, and Express parses them into req.query, while headers carry metadata such as content type and authorisation in req.headers. A GET /users?role=admin request gives req.query.role as 'admin', and req.get('Authorization') reads a single header. Both are strings, so numbers and booleans need parsing before use. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Express query strings and headers — study it before you start the exercise.",
          "syntax": "app.get('/users', (req, res) => {",
