          "concept": "An Express Router groups related routes into a module that the main app mounts with app.use('/users', userRouter). Each router is a mini-app with its own routes and middleware, so a large API stays organised by resource instead of growing into one giant file. Routers can also be nested, which is how /api/v1/users is built from small pieces. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Express routers — study it before you start the exercise.",
