          "concept": "A QuerySet is Django's lazy representation of a database query: Post.objects.filter(published=True) builds the query, and it only hits the database when the results are actually used. Chaining filter, exclude, and order_by refines the query, and values like count() and first() end the chain with a result. Because QuerySets are lazy, building one is cheap and reusing one is safe. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Django QuerySets — study it before you start the exercise.",
