          "concept": "Flask-SQLAlchemy connects Flask to a database through SQLAlchemy's ORM, where a model class maps to a table and db.session commits changes. A model defines columns with db.Column, db.create_all() builds the tables, and queries such as Post.query.filter_by(author='Ada').all() fetch rows as objects. The session is the unit of work: add objects, then commit once, or roll back on error. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Flask-SQLAlchemy — study it before you start the exercise.",
