          "introduction": "OAuth2 and JWT Authentication is a core skill in FastAPI. FastAPI's OAuth2 support reads a bearer token from the Authorization header, and the standard pattern is a JWT that carries the user's id and expiry. In this lesson you will practise FastAPI OAuth2 and JWT with small, runnable examples.",
          "concept": "FastAPI's OAuth2 support reads a bearer token from the Authorization header, and the standard pattern is a JWT that carries the user's id and expiry. A login endpoint checks the password and returns a token, and a get_current_user dependency verifies the token on every protected endpoint. The token is signed with a secret key, so the server can trust it without a database lookup on each request. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with FastAPI OAuth2 and JWT — study it before you start the exercise.",
