          "concept": "A JPA entity is a class annotated with @Entity whose fields map to table columns, and relationships link entities: @ManyToOne for many posts to one author, @OneToMany for the reverse. The owning side holds the foreign key, and cascade settings decide whether saving a parent also saves its children. Lazy loading defers fetching related rows until they are used, which avoids loading the whole database for one query. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Spring JPA entities and relationships — study it before you start the exercise.",
