          "concept": "@ControllerAdvice centralises exception handling: one class with @ExceptionHandler methods turns each exception type into a consistent error response. A ResourceNotFoundException becomes a 404 with a JSON body, while an unexpected exception becomes a 500, and no controller needs its own try/catch. Centralised handling is what makes an API's errors predictable for its clients. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Spring exception handling — study it before you start the exercise.",
