          "introduction": "Queues and Events is a core skill in Laravel. Laravel queues move slow work — sending email, generating reports — out of the request and into a background worker, so the user gets an instant response. In this lesson you will practise Laravel queues and events with small, runnable examples.",
          "concept": "Laravel queues move slow work — sending email, generating reports — out of the request and into a background worker, so the user gets an instant response. A job class holds the work, dispatch() queues it, and php artisan queue:work processes it. Events decouple parts of the app: a UserRegistered event can trigger a welcome email, a log entry, and a stats update without the registration code knowing about them. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Laravel queues and events — study it before you start the exercise.",
