          "concept": "Laravel ships with PHPUnit and test helpers that call routes in-process, assert on responses, and refresh the database between tests. A feature test posts to an endpoint and asserts the status and the database state, which covers the route, the validation, and the model in one call. Deployment runs migrations, caches config and routes, and serves the app from the public folder behind a web server. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Laravel testing and deployment — study it before you start the exercise.",
