          "introduction": "Dependency Injection in Depth is a core skill in ASP.NET Core. ASP.NET Core has dependency injection built in: services are registered in Program.cs with AddScoped, AddSingleton, or AddTransient, and constructors receive them automatically. In this lesson you will practise ASP.NET Core dependency injection with small, runnable examples.",
          "concept": "ASP.NET Core has dependency injection built in: services are registered in Program.cs with AddScoped, AddSingleton, or AddTransient, and constructors receive them automatically. Scoped services live for one request, singletons for the app's lifetime, and transients are created fresh each time. Registering a database context as a singleton is the classic mistake — it is not thread-safe and must be scoped. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with ASP.NET Core dependency injection — study it before you start the exercise.",
          "syntax": "builder.Services.AddScoped<IOrders, OrderService>();",
