          "concept": "Event delegation binds one handler to a parent and lets clicks on any child bubble up to it, which handles elements added later without rebinding. The call is $('ul').on('click', 'li', handler): the parent listens, the selector filters the target, and the handler runs only for matching children. Delegation is the standard answer for dynamic lists, where rebinding after every add is fragile and slow. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with jQuery event delegation — study it before you start the exercise.",
