          "concept": "Traversal walks the DOM from an element: parent() goes up, children() goes down one level, find() searches descendants, and siblings() finds neighbours. jQuery chains these calls, so $(this).closest('li').find('.title') reads like a sentence. Traversal is how a handler finds the data it needs without global ids, which keeps components self-contained. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with DOM traversal — study it before you start the exercise.",
