          "introduction": "The POUR Principles is a core skill in Web Accessibility. The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines organise accessibility into four principles, remembered as POUR: Perceivable, Operable, Understandable, and Robust. In this lesson you will practise POUR accessibility principles with small, runnable examples.",
          "concept": "The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines organise accessibility into four principles, remembered as POUR: Perceivable, Operable, Understandable, and Robust. Perceivable means content can be sensed — text alternatives for images, captions for audio. Operable means it can be used — keyboard access, enough time, no seizure triggers. Understandable means it makes sense, and Robust means it works with assistive technology. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with POUR accessibility principles — study it before you start the exercise.",
