          "concept": "Alt text is the text alternative a screen reader reads for an image, and good alt text conveys the image's message in a sentence or two. Decorative images get an empty alt attribute, alt=\"\", so screen readers skip them instead of announcing a filename. A chart's alt should state its conclusion, not describe every bar — the message matters more than the pixels. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Alt text for images — study it before you start the exercise.",
