          "concept": "Colour contrast is the ratio between text and its background, and WCAG requires at least 4.5:1 for normal text so low-vision readers can read it. Colour must never be the only signal: an error shown only in red is invisible to someone who cannot see red, so pair it with an icon or text. Readable text also means a reasonable size, line spacing, and the ability to zoom to 200% without breaking the layout. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Colour contrast and readable text — study it before you start the exercise.",
