          "concept": "Every form control needs a label, linked with a for attribute matching the input's id, so screen readers announce what the field is for. Placeholder text is not a label: it vanishes when you type, and many screen readers skip it. Error messages must name the field and say how to fix it, and they should be linked to the field with aria-describedby so they are read out. The debugging exercise below shows a typical slip with Accessible forms and labels — study it before you start the exercise.",
          "syntax": "<label for=\"email\">Email address</label>",
          "analogy": "Think of Accessible forms and labels as the backstage crew of a play: invisible when it works, obvious the moment it fails.",
