  "title": "Build a tiny book API",
  "type": "write-code",
  "instructions": "Read book lines 'title:author'. Print each as '{\"title\": \"<title>\", \"author\": \"<author>\"}', one per line, then a final line 'Books: <n>'.",
  "starterCode": "import java.util.*;\nclass Main {\n  public static void main(String[] args) {\n    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n    List<String> lines = new ArrayList<>();\n    while (sc.hasNextLine()) lines.add(sc.nextLine());\n    // Write your code here\n  }\n}\n",
  "solution": "import java.util.*;\nclass Main {\n  public static void main(String[] args) {\n    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n    List<String> lines = new ArrayList<>();\n    while (sc.hasNextLine()) lines.add(sc.nextLine());\n    for (String l : lines) {\n      String[] p = l.split(\":\", 2);\n      System.out.println(\"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"\" + p[0].trim() + \"\\\", \\\"author\\\": \\\"\" + p[1].trim() + \"\\\"}\");\n    }\n    System.out.println(\"Books: \" + lines.size());\n  }\n}\n",
  "solutionExplanation": "Each book is serialised to JSON by the controller, and the count reports the collection size.",
  "complexity": "Medium",
