  "instructions": "SIMULATION (the .NET toolchain is not installed in the sandbox): model this task in Python. Read product lines 'name:price'. Print each as a JSON object {\"name\": \"<name>\", \"price\": <price>}, one per line, then a final line 'Total: <sum>'.",
  "starterCode": "import sys\nlines = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n# Write your code here: read from lines and print the result.\n",
  "solution": "import sys\nlines = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\nimport json\ntotal = 0\nfor l in lines:\n    name, price = l.split(':')\n    total += int(price)\n    print(json.dumps({'name': name, 'price': int(price)}))\nprint('Total: ' + str(total))\n",
